    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0518" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg406"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Northcott.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department has received your No. 14 of
                    the 7th ultimo, relative to the proposed treaty between the United States,
                    Colombia, and Panama, and in reply you are referred to the cabled instructions
                    of October 4 and 23, as defining the department’s attitude on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Huntington Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
